      "text": [
        " : قُلْتُ لِأَبِي عَبْدِ اَللَّهِ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ أَخَذْتُ سُكّاً مِنْ سُكِّ اَلْمَقَامِ وَ تُرَاباً مِنْ تُرَابِ اَلْبَيْتِ وَ سَبْعَ حَصَيَاتٍ فَقَالَ «بِئْسَ مَا صَنَعْتَ أَمَّا اَلتُّرَابَ وَ اَلْحَصَى فَرُدَّهُ »."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.2334 - It has been narrated from Mu'awiyah ibn Ammar, who said:\nI said to Abu Abdullah (as), \"I took some dust from the Maqam and soil from the House, along with seven pebbles.\"\nImam (as) replied: \"What you have done is not good. As for the dust and the pebbles, return them.\""
        ]
      }
